        "notUnderstood": "The \"+2\" under each column is never explained. At the very end I had both waiting slots full and a blue bucket that would return 2, so it jammed with 7 pixels to go. Hard for me to foresee which bucket I should have waited with. The L-tunnel at the top right and the rows of padlocks and keys under the picture still mean nothing to me; they were painted brown without me doing anything.",
        "wouldContinue": true,
        "freeText": "Boss feels like a boss: big 16-19 buckets, five buckets per column, picture is a big blob that I could not recognise until it was finished (a rabbit?). Boss banner (Boss level - The last of the stage, and the hardest.) is readable at 360 wide but overlaps the top edge of the board until closed; the board pixels stay visible. The Masterpiece panel with the stage complete card, new bucket style and the three buttons (Use it now, Next, Album, Map) fits in 360x640 with no cut text, but it is crowded. Jam panel text fits and is clear. +1 slot and continue saved me. Won in 25 moves, one jam, first attempt."
